    "\n  html,body { margin:0; padding:0; font:16px/1.4 -apple-system, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; }\n  /* The three containers this page exists for. Each one holds an ELEMENT at\n     depth 1 and another at depth 2, which is the shape `t0-page.html` lacks:\n     there every hidden container's only descendant is a text node. */\n  #opacity-zero { opacity:0; }\n  #opacity-zero-frame { opacity:0; }\n  #frame-host   { width:300px; height:80px; border:0; }\n  #vis-hidden   { visibility:hidden; }\n  #disp-none    { display:none; }\n  /* A descendant that declares FULL opacity inside the transparent container.\n     CSS group-composites `opacity`, so this element is invisible anyway and\n     cannot re-show itself — unlike `visibility`, where the equivalent\n     declaration really does re-show. Both are measured here. */\n  #op-d2-opaque { opacity:1; }\n  #vis-d2-shown { visibility:visible; }\n  /* A CHAIN BREAK inside the transparent container. A `display:contents` element\n     generates no box, so it gets no DOMSnapshot layout entry and the fetcher has\n     no reading for it at all — while its children are laid out normally. Placed\n     mid-chain (under `#op-d1`, not directly under the container) so that\n     propagating THROUGH it is what the assertion needs, not propagating from an\n     adjacent ancestor. `<slot>` below is the same shape from the UA stylesheet. */\n  #op-contents  { display:contents; }\n  a, button     { cursor:pointer; }\n",
    "BODY",
