    "#comment",
    " OPT-IN, and it stays out of the committed capture deliberately. `?child=<url>` puts a\n         same-origin iframe inside a third `opacity:0` container, which is how the CROSS-FRAME\n         residual is measured: a child document is its own `RawFrame` with its own node array, and\n         `parent` never crosses that boundary. The committed fixture is captured WITHOUT the param\n         so it stays one document; the residual reading is a second run WITH it. ",
    "SCRIPT",
    "\n    // `<slot>` is `display:contents` in the UA stylesheet, which is what makes this chain break\n    // near-universal in component UIs rather than an author's unusual choice: every web component\n    // inside a faded container reaches its slotted light DOM through one.\n    class XFade extends HTMLElement {\n      connectedCallback() {\n        if (this.shadowRoot) return;\n        this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' }).innerHTML = '<div id=\"op-shadow-wrap\"><slot></slot></div>';\n      }\n    }\n    customElements.define('x-fade', XFade);\n\n    var child = new URL(location.href).searchParams.get('child');\n    if (child) { document.getElementById('frame-host').src = child; }\n    else { document.getElementById('opacity-zero-frame').remove(); }\n  ",
    "\n\n\n"
